WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.499
Day-to-day life for the average
Venezuelan is a struggle,

00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:08.042
from the moment you wake up

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:09.669
to the moment you go to sleep.

00:00:11.796 --> 00:00:14.048
From waking up and trying
to turn the lights on,

00:00:14.048 --> 00:00:16.634
to finding out that the
power went out overnight,

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.928
and then trying to take
your morning shower,

00:00:18.928 --> 00:00:21.472
to find out that you
have no water at home.

00:00:22.473 --> 00:00:24.267
Then paying for everything

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:28.104
has become increasingly
complicated, there's no cash.

00:00:29.564 --> 00:00:33.693
Venezuela finding itself
without access to dollars,

00:00:33.693 --> 00:00:34.944
without access to banks,

00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:38.823
without access to avenues of
finance, even for their oil,

00:00:38.823 --> 00:00:41.701
came to the realization, I
guess, that it needed money,

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:44.329
and it needed to find a way to get cash

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:45.580
when most of the world didn't want

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.206
to give 'em access to cash.

00:00:47.206 --> 00:00:52.003
All assets of Maduro,
subject to U.S. jurisdiction,

00:00:52.003 --> 00:00:54.297
are frozen.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.389
So now that U.S. sanctions
have effectively cut off

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:06.434
Maduro's access to a
global financial network,

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:09.646
gold is the last lifeline that Maduro has.

00:01:09.646 --> 00:01:11.272
[Television Announcer] Reports
claim the Maduro regime

00:01:11.272 --> 00:01:13.983
is selling out the country's gold reserves

00:01:13.983 --> 00:01:16.986
to ease the pressure of
international sanctions.

00:01:18.154 --> 00:01:20.948
In the last couple of years, on the side,

00:01:20.948 --> 00:01:22.367
and sort of in secret,

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.994
the Venezuelans and the
Turks started setting up

00:01:24.994 --> 00:01:28.289
a pretty sophisticated web of trade

00:01:28.289 --> 00:01:31.334
of food and gold between
the two countries.

00:01:33.044 --> 00:01:34.253
We're not sure who's winning

00:01:34.253 --> 00:01:35.922
from the sale of Venezuela's gold,

00:01:35.922 --> 00:01:39.050
but what's clear is that the
Venezuelan people are losing.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.428
My name is Michael Smith,

00:01:49.428 --> 00:01:52.168
and I'm a reporter for the
project and investigations team

00:01:52.168 --> 00:01:53.419
here at Bloomberg News.

00:01:53.784 --> 00:01:54.773
My name is Patricia Laya,

00:01:54.773 --> 00:01:56.625
and I'm Bloomberg's
Venezuela bureau chief,

00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:59.628
and I write about Venezuela's
clandestine gold sales.

00:02:01.912 --> 00:02:04.061
So the situation in
Venezuela is really bad,

00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:06.661
and there's currently sort
of two worlds in Venezuela,

00:02:06.661 --> 00:02:10.220
one world is for the people
who have access to dollars.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:13.807
You can probably afford to
have a power generator at home

00:02:13.812 --> 00:02:15.225
in case the power goes out,

00:02:15.228 --> 00:02:18.203
and you can probably have
a water tank installed

00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:20.222
for when there's shortages of water.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.187
Now there's the second
world, that's the world

00:02:24.187 --> 00:02:27.234
that the vast majority
of Venezuelans live in,

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:29.602
and it's the world where
you live in bolivares.

00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:32.901
There's shortages of food,

00:02:32.906 --> 00:02:35.178
inflation runs in the
thousands, tens of thousands,

00:02:35.178 --> 00:02:37.161
hundreds of thousands
percent, nobody really knows.

00:02:37.161 --> 00:02:41.457
Which means, your savings
have long been gone.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:46.426
There's extreme levels of crime

00:02:46.428 --> 00:02:48.586
that makes life extremely difficult

00:02:48.586 --> 00:02:50.755
for anyone who's just
sort of living there.

00:02:53.544 --> 00:02:57.086
You have a whole population
that's subdued by hunger,

00:02:57.086 --> 00:03:00.409
and that's also under the
control of the government,

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:02.369
who's become their sole provider.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.717
People who can't really
think of an economic future

00:03:05.723 --> 00:03:08.726
because they can't think beyond
the day that they're living.

00:03:15.335 --> 00:03:17.289
Nicolas Maduro is a former bus driver

00:03:17.289 --> 00:03:18.749
and a former union leader.

00:03:21.747 --> 00:03:26.625
Maduro came to power in
2013, when Hugo Chavez died.

00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:30.072
And he was basically Chavez's
handpicked successor.

00:03:44.708 --> 00:03:45.904
Outwardly, their message was that

00:03:45.904 --> 00:03:48.124
they wanted to spread
the country's oil wealth

00:03:48.124 --> 00:03:50.818
fairly among the poorest Venezuelans.

00:03:50.818 --> 00:03:52.528
And for a while, they were able to,

00:03:52.536 --> 00:03:54.330
when oil prices were really high,

00:03:54.338 --> 00:03:55.682
they funneled much of that money

00:03:55.682 --> 00:03:57.925
through social programs in Venezuela.

00:03:57.925 --> 00:04:00.428
But they've been heavily corrupted

00:04:00.428 --> 00:04:07.175
in so many different ways,
and bungled, and misapplied,

00:04:07.175 --> 00:04:09.451
that they've really turned into something

00:04:09.451 --> 00:04:12.306
that has just had an
incredibly detrimental effect

00:04:12.306 --> 00:04:15.025
on the people of Venezuela
in many, many different ways.

00:04:15.258 --> 00:04:18.288
And when oil prices crashed,

00:04:18.294 --> 00:04:20.120
the whole economy came crashing down,

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.208
'cause Venezuela depends on
95% of its revenue on oil.

00:04:24.598 --> 00:04:27.375
How bad is it, and is
there any end in sight?

00:04:27.375 --> 00:04:28.826
It's terrible, it's getting worse,

00:04:28.826 --> 00:04:31.621
basically Maduro is
waging economic warfare

00:04:31.646 --> 00:04:33.897
against his own people, his own country.

00:04:33.897 --> 00:04:36.165
An abuse of power that
started with Chavez,

00:04:36.165 --> 00:04:37.991
that allowed him to not just

00:04:37.991 --> 00:04:39.693
change the country's constitution,

00:04:39.693 --> 00:04:42.487
but also fill the country's courts

00:04:42.496 --> 00:04:44.277
and the electoral authority with people

00:04:44.277 --> 00:04:45.611
that were loyal to him,

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.532
and that allowed the country

00:04:48.532 --> 00:04:53.049
to completely eliminate any
sort of democratic institution.

00:04:53.049 --> 00:04:56.281
Maduro has given most of
the government's control

00:04:56.281 --> 00:04:57.277
to the military,

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.721
so the feeling is that, if
Maduro falls, they fall.

00:05:01.721 --> 00:05:07.221
So, they have formed a bond
through money laundering,

00:05:07.221 --> 00:05:11.841
fraud, and all sorts
of illegal businesses.

00:05:11.883 --> 00:05:13.763
[Television Reporter] A
first shipment of gold bars

00:05:13.765 --> 00:05:16.881
has arrived in Venezuela
after President Hugo Chavez

00:05:16.881 --> 00:05:19.759
recalled almost all the country's
foreign bullion reserves

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:21.177
from western banks.

00:05:21.203 --> 00:05:25.439
So in 2011, shortly after
the US economic crisis

00:05:25.439 --> 00:05:27.000
and the European debt crisis,

00:05:27.004 --> 00:05:29.175
Chavez basically used that as an excuse

00:05:29.175 --> 00:05:31.459
to have about 11 billion worth

00:05:31.459 --> 00:05:35.663
of Venezuela's gold repatriated
from banks in North America,

00:05:35.663 --> 00:05:38.059
banks in Europe, back to Venezuela.

00:05:38.059 --> 00:05:40.585
He said that it was a measure to safeguard

00:05:40.587 --> 00:05:44.817
against financial
instability around the world.

00:05:44.817 --> 00:05:48.218
And that move by Chavez
almost a decade ago

00:05:48.218 --> 00:05:53.023
is what's keeping Maduro
selling gold nowadays.

00:05:53.023 --> 00:05:55.818
It's legal for Maduro to sell his gold,

00:05:55.824 --> 00:05:58.626
but what's happened is
that after U.S. sanctions,

00:05:58.626 --> 00:06:01.153
a lot of the buyers have been spooked.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.553
So what's happened is that

00:06:02.553 --> 00:06:05.542
they've begun to sell the gold in secrecy.

00:06:05.542 --> 00:06:08.128
[Reporter] On Venezuela, you did the tough sanctions

00:06:08.128 --> 00:06:09.775
and you sent the aid,

00:06:09.775 --> 00:06:13.670
but it seems like Maduro
is no closer to leaving.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.029
We really haven't done the
really tough sanctions yet.

00:06:16.032 --> 00:06:18.497
We can do the tough sanctions
and all options are open.

00:06:18.497 --> 00:06:20.069
We want Maduro to leave

00:06:20.069 --> 00:06:22.169
so there can be free and fair elections,

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:24.484
with the ultimate goal of ensuring

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:26.882
that there's democracy
and freedom in Venezuela.

00:06:28.892 --> 00:06:31.994
The U.S. has imposed sanctions on Venezuela

00:06:31.994 --> 00:06:33.164
more than a decade ago,

00:06:33.171 --> 00:06:35.156
but they never went further

00:06:35.156 --> 00:06:39.892
than individual targeted
sanctions until 2017.

00:06:39.892 --> 00:06:41.894
We have our eye very closely on Venezuela,

00:06:42.306 --> 00:06:43.671
Since President Trump

00:06:43.671 --> 00:06:44.826
took office,

00:06:44.827 --> 00:06:47.019
they were just accelerated
to cover hundreds of people

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:50.382
and companies and government entities

00:06:50.385 --> 00:06:51.867
and that sort of thing.

00:06:51.867 --> 00:06:54.457
We have continued to expose the corruption

00:06:54.457 --> 00:06:57.960
of Maduro and his cronies
and today's action ensures

00:06:57.982 --> 00:07:01.485
they can no longer loot the
assets of the Venezuelan people.

00:07:01.742 --> 00:07:06.622
US sanctions can be
devastating for the people

00:07:06.624 --> 00:07:07.990
and companies that are targeted,

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.286
they're listed and targets of sanctions.

00:07:11.287 --> 00:07:16.904
You become a pariah in the
system of commerce and finance.

00:07:16.942 --> 00:07:19.111
Unless you're in a country

00:07:19.128 --> 00:07:23.882
that will allow you to do
business despite US sanctions,

00:07:23.882 --> 00:07:25.801
and that's what's going on with Turkey.

00:07:26.826 --> 00:07:28.777
[News Anchor] Let's get straight to the
breaking news overnight.

00:07:28.786 --> 00:07:31.324
An attempted coup leading to chaos, death,

00:07:31.324 --> 00:07:33.288
and instability in Turkey.

00:07:33.288 --> 00:07:35.525
In July of 2016,

00:07:35.525 --> 00:07:37.500
there was a coup attempt in Turkey

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.922
against the government President Erdogan,

00:07:40.922 --> 00:07:43.856
and it was a serious material threat

00:07:43.856 --> 00:07:45.107
to the Erdogan government.

00:07:45.274 --> 00:07:46.217
The US watching

00:07:46.217 --> 00:07:48.427
this sudden uprising with concern.

00:07:48.427 --> 00:07:50.460
Erdogan felt isolated,

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.920
he wasn't getting much support

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.265
from anyone in the world that day,

00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:55.740
and one of the first calls he got

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.896
was from a representative of
the Venezuelan government,

00:07:58.896 --> 00:08:02.286
who contacted the Turkish
embassy in Venezuela,

00:08:02.286 --> 00:08:04.782
and said, "We're with you,

00:08:04.782 --> 00:08:09.704
we know what it's like to be
a victim of a coup attempt,

00:08:09.715 --> 00:08:12.093
we're pretty sure the U.S.
government was behind it somewhat,

00:08:12.095 --> 00:08:13.714
we're with you."

00:08:13.714 --> 00:08:16.300
And that contact,

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:20.017
which went all the way up to
the president of Venezuela

00:08:20.017 --> 00:08:21.717
and the president of Turkey,

00:08:21.719 --> 00:08:23.148
was really sort of the seed

00:08:23.148 --> 00:08:28.373
that turned into a conduit
for the Venezuelans

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:30.525
to get their gold out of the country,

00:08:30.525 --> 00:08:31.987
and to turn it into money.

00:08:37.476 --> 00:08:40.766
There's been a tremendous trade of gold,

00:08:40.766 --> 00:08:43.346
tons and tons and tons and tons of it,

00:08:43.346 --> 00:08:46.427
that has left Venezuela,

00:08:46.427 --> 00:08:48.345
a lot of the national
reserves have been sold off.

00:08:48.386 --> 00:08:51.387
He still has this lifeline
that's available to him,

00:08:51.387 --> 00:08:54.182
and that he's clearly been
able to get away with.

00:08:54.819 --> 00:08:58.781
We've seen him do a multitude
of gold sales this year,

00:08:58.781 --> 00:09:00.741
despite the sanctions that are in place,

00:09:00.741 --> 00:09:03.160
so they realized that he still has a way

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.830
to prop up his regime
and to stay in power.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.575
There is an estimated eighty tonnes 
left at the central bank.

00:09:15.575 --> 00:09:20.450
That's about $3.5 billion worth.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.477
What's left right now is only
enough for six more months

00:09:25.477 --> 00:09:27.587
of food subsidies for Venezuela's people,

00:09:27.587 --> 00:09:29.701
so if Venezuela runs out of gold,

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:31.869
we don't really know
what's going to happen.

00:09:35.112 --> 00:09:39.032
What we do know is that they
are feeling the pressure,

00:09:39.049 --> 00:09:43.231
and this pressure of knowing
that gold can soon run out

00:09:43.231 --> 00:09:46.113
is what's bringing them to
negotiate with the opposition.

00:09:46.359 --> 00:09:48.839
To predict where things
are going in Venezuela

00:09:48.839 --> 00:09:51.467
is a dangerous game in my experience.

00:09:51.756 --> 00:09:53.007
You could always find people saying,

00:09:53.007 --> 00:09:54.503
"Oh, this can't go on any longer,

00:09:54.503 --> 00:09:55.955
it's gonna collapse,"

00:09:55.955 --> 00:10:00.960
but I think it's a very
complex crisis there

00:10:00.965 --> 00:10:05.119
and it's gonna be very
difficult to find a solution

00:10:05.119 --> 00:10:07.333
that really works quickly, I think.

